{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011E4oUDXiker2QSeHNuaYCH","type":"tool_result","content":"# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal:\nagent\nagentjob\nbotcheck\nbudget\ncli\ncloseout\ncommitter\nconfig\nconfigcmd\nconfigsrc\ncontroller\ncostblock\ncosts\neffects\nexecutor\ngithub\ngitref\ngitx\ninitcmd\nintake\njanitor\nlabels\nlimits\nmerger\nmodelauth\npool\nprgate\nreaper\nredact\nrepopath\nreviewer\nreviewfix\nroles\nscanner\nservecmd\nstate\ntriage\nworker\nwtlock\n\ninternal/config:\nafter.go\nafter_test.go\nbudget_test.go\ndefaults.go\ndiscover.go\nduration.go\nduration_test.go\nerrors.go\nload.go\nload_test.go\nprotected.go\nprotected_test.go\nraw.go\nrender.go\nrender_test.go\nroot.go\nselect.go\nsource.go\nsource_test.go\ntestdata\ntypes.go\nwhen_test.go\n\ninternal/reaper:\ndecide.go\ndecide_test.go\ndoc.go\nfinish.go\nfinishwith_test.go\nharness_test.go\nlimit.go\nlimit_test.go\nnorecord.go\nreaper.go\nreaper_test.go\nretention.go\nusage_test.go\n\ninternal/state:\nadmissions.go\nadmissions_test.go\ncosttables.go\ncosttables_test.go\ndir.go\ndir_test.go\nevents.go\ngolden_test.go\njobs.go\nmigrations\nreaper_test.go\nscannerdb\nsqlitex\nstore.go\nstore_test.go\ntestdata\nusage.go\nusage_test.go\n01M850CGZMWWE6P01JDDWD7JSR.json\n01M85A4HX3P7Q5W8SSHSWN3FT8.json\n     104 internal/state/admissions.go\n      44 internal/state/admissions_test.go\n      86 internal/state/costtables.go\n     111 internal/state/costtables_test.go\n      89 internal/state/dir.go\n      76 internal/state/dir_test.go\n     169 internal/state/events.go\n      56 internal/state/golden_test.go\n     709 internal/state/jobs.go\n     344 internal/state/reaper_test.go\n     111 internal/state/store.go\n     446 internal/state/store_test.go\n     236 internal/state/usage.go\n     166 internal/state/usage_test.go\n      75 internal/reaper/decide.go\n     161 internal/reaper/decide_test.go\n      63 internal/reaper/doc.go\n     394 internal/reaper/finish.go\n      94 internal/reaper/finishwith_test.go\n     410 internal/reaper/harness_test.go\n      83 internal/reaper/limit.go\n     419 internal/reaper/limit_test.go\n     158 internal/reaper/norecord.go\n     394 internal/reaper/reaper.go\n     871 internal/reaper/reaper_test.go\n      89 internal/reaper/retention.go\n     182 internal/reaper/usage_test.go\n      56 internal/config/after.go\n      40 internal/config/after_test.g